            <div xml:id="d730">

                <pb facs="0650" n="641" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg641"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/5299: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Leopoldville</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Mallon</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Leopoldville</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-08-28T16:00:00+01:00">August 28, 1940—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 28—3:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to my telegram of this morning, Husson, Governor General of French
                    Equatorial Africa, physically attacked by pro-De Gaulle faction escaped to
                    Leopoldville and has sought refuge with the Governor General of the Belgian
                    Congo. The whole of French Equatorial Africa has now declared for De Gaulle. De
                    Larminat has gone to Brazzaville.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mallon</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
